  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.request_peer_binding (no source diff) and proxy.transport_binding_application. transport/ingress/v2.rs now takes the node's trust as one LbAssertionV2Trust and splits LbAssertionV2Binding::verify into check_signature, check_freshness, check_route, check_request_binding, admit_recorded_facts and verified; the steps run in the same order (key lookup and signature, freshness and expiry, request binding, audience, ingress identity, recorded facts) with the same rejection for each, and the same revocation outcomes. Peer-to-subject binding in request_peer_binding is unchanged. The claim, premises and dependencies are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor, and every tested symbol the unit names still names a test function. The previous record named the owner as reviewer; it is replaced because its fingerprint no longer matched the tree, and it remains in git history. Owner ratification of this reading is the owner's act.",
